      "message": "But this is the expected result with any merge submit strategy (which suggests perhaps we need tests for conflicts operator and other submit strategies). commit4 won\u0027t submit without commit1 submitting first, so there can never be a conflict. You can\u0027t conflict with anything in your history. It\u0027s not a false negative, it\u0027s a true negative.\n\nThe case where this gets interesting is when change1 has a newer patchset that is no longer commit1. If that new commit5 has anything other than `v1` in `shared`, then I would expect change1 to show up in `conflicts:4`, indicating a trivial rebase isn\u0027t possible.",
